  "body": "## Result and exact scope\n\nAdds only `research/complex-heterogeneous-child-interface/`: a complete **unequal-width** classification for one inherited Clifford tensor child under arbitrary reciprocal linear encoding, plus exact source and volume accounting.\n\nFor two equal-volume lanes with canonical operators `C_p` and `C_q^epsilon`, `1 <= p < q`, and a candidate child `lambda C_d tensor I_t` with positive integers **d>=1, t>=1**, arbitrary restored dirty identity padding does not help. Width-zero scalar children are outside this declared contract:\n\n- Same directions never fit one phased child, even granting arbitrary invertible encoding and its inverse.\n- Opposite directions fit exactly when `q=p+1` and `p=1 or 2 mod4`, or `q=p+2` and `p=1 mod4`. The child width is necessarily `q+2`, with the explicit phase in the proof, and its active volume is the sum of both original lane volumes.\n- Three full rational basis witnesses attain the exceptional cases. For example, `(C_1 tensor I_4) direct-sum (C_2^-1 tensor I_2)` is similar to `-C_4` on 16 coordinates.\n- Even with both encoders and every other extra charge free, the inherited available child expression `2 A V(q+2)^sigma` exceeds `A V(p^sigma+q^sigma)` for `0<sigma<1`. This is an **upper-bound-expression comparison**, not an optimal-runtime lower bound.\n\nThe proof uses Gaussian-prime valuation to force the new width and exact four-trace multiplicities for necessity/sufficiency. It is not extrapolation from the finite sweep.\n\n## Concrete source connection and predecessor credit\n\nAn independent scan of both 24,767-event selected local orientations reconstructs all 359 higher-rank same-ADD pairs from PR1836, and binds all **215 heterogeneous pairs** by source gate, rational coefficient, old/new frame and quotient ranks. None of those 215 same-direction canonical substitutions is realized by the declared reciprocal packing route, at any positive column multiplicity. The 144 equal-rank rows and their prior reciprocal obstruction remain PR1920's credit.\n\nThe scope fixes the original per-lane normal-form endpoint charts. It does not infer that the original physical frame charts are reciprocal, or exclude independent nonreciprocal adapters, clean invariant encodings, a different joint primitive, or a new child tariff. PR1836 already labels its supplier unadmitted; this resolves a specific route rather than alleging that its conditional screen was a construction.\n\nNearest work:\n- PR1836 `0a62e3f1c0ea493ddb83f25b91c5548c87978bcc`: census and hypothetical rank-sum screen (Cinna Davis).\n- PR1920 `057b214aea45c65926b93ad8b95693c80f0f79c9`: equal-width reciprocal obstruction/exceptions and volume comparison (Arham Tahir).\n- PR1924 `0a7c54dd94bce3784b61c4203adfdda98d13d53d`: different clean-invariant-subspace contract (ToikY).\n- PR1866 `7d22d1d51eb6c0bc040f8181b6c5f83e051fb234`: different heterogeneous bilinear tensor, not this Clifford operator.\n- PR679 and PR1240: inherited volume tariff and exact ceiling engine; icekylinx and the selected Rohan Arun/Jeremy Kothe/Hao Yan source lineage are retained.\n\nThe counterfactual 215-pair-only profile is also screened exactly: baseline cap bracket `[0.001690054109,0.001690054110]`; hypothetical bracket `[0.001733875133,0.001733875134]`. It does not clear 5%, and it is not an admitted profile. **No supplier, new kappa, selected-record or frozen-source change.**\n\n## Reproduction and exercised evidence\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -B research/complex-heterogeneous-child-interface/verify.py\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -O -B research/complex-heterogeneous-child-interface/verify.py\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/complex-heterogeneous-child-interface\n```\n\nObserved on CPython 3.12.12, macOS 27.0.1 arm64, standard library only:\n\n```text\nPASS_HETEROGENEOUS_CHILD_INTERFACE spectral_trials=747264 matches=48 heterogeneous_gates=215 fixtures=3 controls=9 no_new_kappa\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/complex-heterogeneous-child-interface outcome=negative-result\n```\n\nThe sweep covers unequal widths through 64, candidate widths through q+3, both directions and all four phases. It cross-checks cyclic/binomial spectra through 67, signed reductions, three complete rational encoding matrices (2304 operator entries), both source orientations, nine named controls and six additional matrix negative witnesses. Normal receipt generation, optimized read-only replay and registered replay all passed. The card's ceiling working example and lever table also passed. Exact commands, hashes, environment and unrun obligations are in `VALIDATION.json`.\n\nNo full selected cold replay, native hosting/adapters, proof assistant, hosted CI success or independent human review is claimed. The all-width theorem is written mathematics.\n\n## Independent task provenance\n\nRound 2 instance 05, exact base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`; OS-random chooser sampled once with no overrides. Seed `c2889b6f0505155ec921e731269f82bf`, track `complex-mechanisms`, selected emitted card `complex-rank-shape-decoder`. Complete selection is preserved in `SELECTION.json`. TASK records the explicit scope change from physical synthesis to this prerequisite interface theorem and cost screen.\n\nClaim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1929#discussioncomment-18926013\n\nFinal shared overlap covered 584 open PRs and 565 Discussion records with complete pagination; targeted current heads and local/merged notes were also checked. Metadata search is not a novelty certificate.\n\nPrepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in mathematics, research, implementation, checking and writing. Apache-2.0. The next useful question is a fully priced nonreciprocal adapter, not another reciprocal basis search.\n",
